# Beginner PCB Design Project

This project represents my first hands-on experience with PCB design as an Electronics and Communication Engineering (ECE) student.

## Project Overview
- Designed a basic electronic circuit schematic
- Converted the schematic into a PCB layout
- Learned component placement, routing, and PCB design basics
- Understood beginner-level PCB design mistakes and corrections

## Components Used
- ESP32-WROOM-32UE
- OLED Display (SSD1306)
- DHT22 Sensor
- MQ Gas Sensor
- AMS1117 Voltage Regulator
- USB Type-C Connector
- Capacitors and Resistors

## Tools Used
- EasyEDA (PCB Design Software)
- Basic Electronic Components
- GitHub for Project Documentation

## Project Files Included
- PCB Top Layer Design
- PCB Bottom Layer Design
- 3D PCB View
- Circuit Schematic PDF
- Bill of Materials (BOM)

## What I Learned
- Reading and understanding datasheets
- Schematic creation
- Footprint assignment
- PCB routing and layout basics
- Importance of grounding and track width
- Debugging PCB design errors
- Copper pour and GND plane implementation

## Project Outcome
This project helped me build confidence in hardware design and motivated me to learn more about real-world PCB development and embedded systems.

